  "notes": "Stetson University operates on a course-unit system (1 unit = 4 semester hours; the catalog's course descriptions print '1 Unit' per standard course). All credit values here are the catalog's unit values converted x4 and shown as credits (e.g. 1 unit = 4 credits, 0.5 units = 2 credits, 0.0 units = 0 credits). Semester declared_credits are the catalog's printed 'Term Units' converted likewise, and they equal the converted course-credit sums. The plan is a 'suggested sequence' per pipeline rules. Source: Stetson University 2026-2027 Academic Catalog, 'Advising Course Plan - Biology Major - Medical School Interest', Plan #1 (bio-med-sch-plan.pdf, current catalog). Plan #1 'was developed ... and indicates an effective way to earn a Bachelor of Science degree in Biology and to complete the typical premedical requirements without taking two lab sciences in year 1' (suggested sequence). The catalog also publishes a Plan #2 accelerated variant (two lab sciences in year 1, MCAT after third year) — not collected here. BIOL 499 prints as '0.5 to 1' units: genuine catalog range resolved at the minimum (0.5 units = 2 credits) with this disclosure; program total 31.5 units = 126 credits. Course codes/titles/units verbatim from the plan PDF and catalog course descriptions; prereq arrays are empty (not published in the plan; not invented). Catalog footnotes: math timing not critical (MATH 130/141Q placement); PSYC 101S and/or SOCI 101S can be taken any time before the MCAT; Junior Seminar can move to spring; spring of third/fourth year may need another 0.5- or 1-unit course to average 4 units/semester; consider CHEM 304 in spring of fourth year (catalog suggestion). No TCCNS in Florida; transfer_confidence is empty.",
